--TEST--
A string converted with `as propertyPath<T>` while the program runs is checked one part at a time, and a part that names nothing, names a private property, continues after a property that is not an object, or is empty throws an error that names it; a path that loops back to a class is valid at any length — `rule:types/property-path`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// A path from a string is checked when it is converted.
// A bad part throws an error that names the part.
class Category {
    public string $name = "Books";
    public ?Category $parent = null;
    private string $secret = "s";
}

class Product {
    public Category $category;
    public int $price = 5;

    public function constructor() {
        $this->category = new Category();
    }
}

class Check {
    public static function path(string $text): void {
        try {
            propertyPath<Product> $path = $text as propertyPath<Product>;
            echo "valid: ", $path as string, "\n";
        } catch (Throwable $e) {
            echo $e->message, "\n";
        }
    }
}

Check::path("category.name");
Check::path("category.nmae");
Check::path("category.secret");
Check::path("price.amount");
Check::path("category..name");

// `parent` is a `?Category`, so a path can repeat it many times.
string $long = "category";
for (int $i = 0; $i < 200; $i++) {
    $long = $long . ".parent";
}
propertyPath<Product> $deep = ($long . ".name") as propertyPath<Product>;
echo Core\Str::length($deep as string), "\n";
// covers: lang:types/property-paths
--EXPECT--
valid: category.name
`"category.nmae"` is not a property path of `Product`: `Category` has no public property `$nmae`
`"category.secret"` is not a property path of `Product`: `Category` has no public property `$secret`
`"price.amount"` is not a property path of `Product`: `Product`'s property `$price` is not an object, so the path cannot continue after it
`"category..name"` is not a property path of `Product`: it has an empty part
1413
